---Summary information for a Amazon Kendra data source.
---@class aws.kendra.DataSourceSummary
---@field Name? aws.kendra.DataSourceName The name of the data source.
---@field Id? aws.kendra.DataSourceId The identifier for the data source.
---@field Type? aws.kendra.DataSourceType The type of the data source.
---@field CreatedAt? aws.kendra.Timestamp The Unix timestamp when the data source connector was created.
---@field UpdatedAt? aws.kendra.Timestamp The Unix timestamp when the data source connector was last updated.
---@field Status? aws.kendra.DataSourceStatus The status of the data source. When the status is ACTIVE the data source is ready to use.
---@field LanguageCode? aws.kendra.LanguageCode The code for a language. This shows a supported language for all documents in the data source. English is supported by default. For more information on supported languages, including their codes, see Adding documents in languages other than English.

---@alias aws.kendra.DataSourceSummaryList aws.kendra.DataSourceSummary[]

---Provides information about a data source synchronization job.
---@class aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJob
---@field ExecutionId? aws.kendra.String A identifier for the synchronization job.
---@field StartTime? aws.kendra.Timestamp The Unix timestamp when the synchronization job started.
---@field EndTime? aws.kendra.Timestamp The Unix timestamp when the synchronization job completed.
---@field Status? aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobStatus The execution status of the synchronization job. When the Status field is set to SUCCEEDED, the synchronization job is done. If the status code is set to FAILED, the ErrorCode and ErrorMessage fields give you the reason for the failure.
---@field ErrorMessage? aws.kendra.ErrorMessage If the Status field is set to ERROR, the ErrorMessage field contains a description of the error that caused the synchronization to fail.
---@field ErrorCode? aws.kendra.ErrorCode If the Status field is set to FAILED, the ErrorCode field indicates the reason the synchronization failed.
---@field DataSourceErrorCode? aws.kendra.String If the reason that the synchronization failed is due to an error with the underlying data source, this field contains a code that identifies the error.
---@field Metrics? aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobMetrics Maps a batch delete document request to a specific data source sync job. This is optional and should only be supplied when documents are deleted by a data source connector.

---@alias aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobHistoryList aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJob[]

---@alias aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobId string

---Maps a particular data source sync job to a particular data source.
---@class aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobMetricTarget
---@field DataSourceId aws.kendra.DataSourceId The ID of the data source that is running the sync job.
---@field DataSourceSyncJobId? aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobId The ID of the sync job that is running on the data source.

---Maps a batch delete document request to a specific data source sync job. This is optional and should only be supplied when documents are deleted by a data source connector.
---@class aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobMetrics
---@field DocumentsAdded? aws.kendra.MetricValue The number of documents added from the data source up to now in the data source sync.
---@field DocumentsModified? aws.kendra.MetricValue The number of documents modified in the data source up to now in the data source sync run.
---@field DocumentsDeleted? aws.kendra.MetricValue The number of documents deleted from the data source up to now in the data source sync run.
---@field DocumentsFailed? aws.kendra.MetricValue The number of documents that failed to sync from the data source up to now in the data source sync run.
---@field DocumentsScanned? aws.kendra.MetricValue The current number of documents crawled by the current sync job in the data source.

---@alias aws.kendra.DataSourceSyncJobStatus "FAILED"|"SUCCEEDED"|"SYNCING"|"INCOMPLETE"|"STOPPING"|"ABORTED"|"SYNCING_INDEXING"

---Maps attributes or field names of the documents synced from the data source to Amazon Kendra index field names. You can set up field mappings for each data source when calling CreateDataSource or UpdateDataSource API. To create custom fields, use the UpdateIndex API to first create an index field and then map to the data source field. For more information, see Mapping data source fields.
---@class aws.kendra.DataSourceToIndexFieldMapping
