---@class aws.kendra.QueryRequest
---@field IndexId aws.kendra.IndexId The identifier of the index for the search.
---@field QueryText? aws.kendra.QueryText The input query text for the search. Amazon Kendra truncates queries at 30 token words, which excludes punctuation and stop words. Truncation still applies if you use Boolean or more advanced, complex queries. For example, Timeoff AND October AND Category:HR is counted as 3 tokens: timeoff, october, hr. For more information, see Searching with advanced query syntax in the Amazon Kendra Developer G...
---@field AttributeFilter? aws.kendra.AttributeFilter Filters search results by document fields/attributes. You can only provide one attribute filter; however, the AndAllFilters, NotFilter, and OrAllFilters parameters contain a list of other filters.
---@field Facets? aws.kendra.FacetList An array of documents fields/attributes for faceted search. Amazon Kendra returns a count for each field key specified. This helps your users narrow their search.
---@field RequestedDocumentAttributes? aws.kendra.DocumentAttributeKeyList An array of document fields/attributes to include in the response. You can limit the response to include certain document fields. By default, all document attributes are included in the response.
---@field QueryResultTypeFilter? aws.kendra.QueryResultType|string Sets the type of query result or response. Only results for the specified type are returned.
---@field DocumentRelevanceOverrideConfigurations? aws.kendra.DocumentRelevanceOverrideConfigurationList Overrides relevance tuning configurations of fields/attributes set at the index level.
---@field PageNumber? aws.kendra.Integer Query results are returned in pages the size of the PageSize parameter. By default, Amazon Kendra returns the first page of results. Use this parameter to get result pages after the first one.
---@field PageSize? aws.kendra.Integer Sets the number of results that are returned in each page of results. The default page size is 10. The maximum number of results returned is 100. If you ask for more than 100 results, only 100 are returned.
---@field SortingConfiguration? aws.kendra.SortingConfiguration Provides information that determines how the results of the query are sorted. You can set the field that Amazon Kendra should sort the results on, and specify whether the results should be sorted in ascending or descending order. In the case of ties in sorting the results, the results are sorted by relevance.
---@field SortingConfigurations? aws.kendra.SortingConfigurationList Provides configuration information to determine how the results of a query are sorted.
---@field UserContext? aws.kendra.UserContext The user context token or user and group information.
---@field VisitorId? aws.kendra.VisitorId Provides an identifier for a specific user. The VisitorId should be a unique identifier, such as a GUID. Don't use personally identifiable information, such as the user's email address, as the VisitorId.
---@field SpellCorrectionConfiguration? aws.kendra.SpellCorrectionConfiguration Enables suggested spell corrections for queries.
---@field CollapseConfiguration? aws.kendra.CollapseConfiguration Provides configuration to determine how to group results by document attribute value, and how to display them (collapsed or expanded) under a designated primary document for each group.

---@class aws.kendra.QueryResult
---@field QueryId? aws.kendra.QueryId The identifier for the search. You also use QueryId to identify the search when using the SubmitFeedback API.
---@field ResultItems? aws.kendra.QueryResultItemList The results of the search.
---@field FacetResults? aws.kendra.FacetResultList Contains the facet results. A FacetResult contains the counts for each field/attribute key that was specified in the Facets input parameter.
---@field TotalNumberOfResults? aws.kendra.Integer The total number of items found by the search. However, you can only retrieve up to 100 items. For example, if the search found 192 items, you can only retrieve the first 100 of the items.
---@field Warnings? aws.kendra.WarningList A list of warning codes and their messages on problems with your query.
---@field SpellCorrectedQueries? aws.kendra.SpellCorrectedQueryList A list of information related to suggested spell corrections for a query.
---@field FeaturedResultsItems? aws.kendra.FeaturedResultsItemList The list of featured result items. Featured results are displayed at the top of the search results page, placed above all other results for certain queries. If there's an exact match of a query, then certain documents are featured in the search results.

---@alias aws.kendra.QueryResultFormat "TABLE"|"TEXT"

---A single query result.
---@class aws.kendra.QueryResultItem
---@field Id? aws.kendra.ResultId The unique identifier for the query result item id (Id) and the query result item document id (DocumentId) combined. The value of this field changes with every request, even when you have the same documents.
---@field Type? aws.kendra.QueryResultType The type of document within the response. For example, a response could include a question-answer that's relevant to the query.
---@field Format? aws.kendra.QueryResultFormat If the Type of document within the response is ANSWER, then it is either a TABLE answer or TEXT answer. If it's a table answer, a table excerpt is returned in TableExcerpt. If it's a text answer, a text excerpt is returned in DocumentExcerpt.
---@field AdditionalAttributes? aws.kendra.AdditionalResultAttributeList One or more additional fields/attributes associated with the query result.
---@field DocumentId? aws.kendra.DocumentId The identifier for the document.
---@field DocumentTitle? aws.kendra.TextWithHighlights The title of the document. Contains the text of the title and information for highlighting the relevant terms in the title.
---@field DocumentExcerpt? aws.kendra.TextWithHighlights An extract of the text in the document. Contains information about highlighting the relevant terms in the excerpt.
---@field DocumentURI? aws.kendra.Url The URI of the original location of the document.
---@field DocumentAttributes? aws.kendra.DocumentAttributeList An array of document fields/attributes assigned to a document in the search results. For example, the document author (_author) or the source URI (_source_uri) of the document.
---@field ScoreAttributes? aws.kendra.ScoreAttributes Indicates the confidence level of Amazon Kendra providing a relevant result for the query. Each result is placed into a bin that indicates the confidence, VERY_HIGH, HIGH, MEDIUM and LOW. You can use the score to determine if a response meets the confidence needed for your application.
---@field FeedbackToken? aws.kendra.FeedbackToken A token that identifies a particular result from a particular query. Use this token to provide click-through feedback for the result. For more information, see Submitting feedback.
---@field TableExcerpt? aws.kendra.TableExcerpt An excerpt from a table within a document.
---@field CollapsedResultDetail? aws.kendra.CollapsedResultDetail Provides details about a collapsed group of search results.

---@alias aws.kendra.QueryResultItemList aws.kendra.QueryResultItem[]

