---Provides the configuration information to connect to Slack as your data source.
---@class aws.kendra.SlackConfiguration
---@field TeamId aws.kendra.TeamId The identifier of the team in the Slack workspace. For example, T0123456789.
---@field SecretArn aws.kendra.SecretArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an Secrets Manager secret that contains the key-value pairs required to connect to your Slack workspace team. The secret must contain a JSON structure with the following keys:
---@field VpcConfiguration? aws.kendra.DataSourceVpcConfiguration Configuration information for an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud to connect to your Slack. For more information, see Configuring a VPC.
---@field SlackEntityList aws.kendra.SlackEntityList Specify whether to index public channels, private channels, group messages, and direct messages. You can specify one or more of these options.
---@field UseChangeLog? aws.kendra.Boolean TRUE to use the Slack change log to determine which documents require updating in the index. Depending on the Slack change log's size, it may take longer for Amazon Kendra to use the change log than to scan all of your documents in Slack.
---@field CrawlBotMessage? aws.kendra.Boolean TRUE to index bot messages from your Slack workspace team.
---@field ExcludeArchived? aws.kendra.Boolean TRUE to exclude archived messages to index from your Slack workspace team.
---@field SinceCrawlDate aws.kendra.SinceCrawlDate The date to start crawling your data from your Slack workspace team. The date must follow this format: yyyy-mm-dd.
---@field LookBackPeriod? aws.kendra.LookBackPeriod The number of hours for change log to look back from when you last synchronized your data. You can look back up to 7 days or 168 hours.
---@field PrivateChannelFilter? aws.kendra.PrivateChannelFilter The list of private channel names from your Slack workspace team. You use this if you want to index specific private channels, not all private channels. You can also use regular expression patterns to filter private channels.
---@field PublicChannelFilter? aws.kendra.PublicChannelFilter The list of public channel names to index from your Slack workspace team. You use this if you want to index specific public channels, not all public channels. You can also use regular expression patterns to filter public channels.
---@field InclusionPatterns? aws.kendra.DataSourceInclusionsExclusionsStrings A list of regular expression patterns to include certain attached files in your Slack workspace team. Files that match the patterns are included in the index. Files that don't match the patterns are excluded from the index. If a file matches both an inclusion and exclusion pattern, the exclusion pattern takes precedence and the file isn't included in the index.
---@field ExclusionPatterns? aws.kendra.DataSourceInclusionsExclusionsStrings A list of regular expression patterns to exclude certain attached files in your Slack workspace team. Files that match the patterns are excluded from the index. Files that don’t match the patterns are included in the index. If a file matches both an inclusion and exclusion pattern, the exclusion pattern takes precedence and the file isn't included in the index.
---@field FieldMappings? aws.kendra.DataSourceToIndexFieldMappingList A list of DataSourceToIndexFieldMapping objects that map Slack data source attributes or field names to Amazon Kendra index field names. To create custom fields, use the UpdateIndex API before you map to Slack fields. For more information, see Mapping data source fields. The Slack data source field names must exist in your Slack custom metadata.

